            <ArticleTitle>Arrhythmogenic right ventricular dysplasia presenting with severe right heart failure leading to abdominal ascites in a child.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>546-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This report describes a 12-year-old girl with arrhythmogenic right ventricular dysplasia, presenting with severe right ventricular failure symptoms including fatigue, abdominal pain and distension due to abdominal ascites.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
